{
  "$schema": "../scene.schema.json",
  "id": "briar-glen-green",
  "name": "Briar Glen: Market Green",
  "description": "Bead mw-e24.2: the rest of Briar Glen, a grey-box town square about 180 x 140 m behind the shop lane (briar-glen-lane stays the lane district; this scene is its second district, reached by the lane-gate transition from the lane's north end, the green-gate stub beside the woodside path; arrive-from-briar-glen-lane stands inside the west gate). Market Green is the open square in the middle (notice-board, the Glen Well with its loose-rung marker, stalls and street lanterns). Round it: the Lamplit Stacks on the west side, three storeys that visibly lean to the west onto the brands-forge-yard annex (the Forge's rear smithy, whose counter and front are in the lane); the Watch House on the north side; the schoolhouse on the east side; the lychgate cemetery south-east; and Vane House on a four metre rise in the north-east, reached by a broad stair, its 40 m tower the tallest thing in town so it can be seen from everywhere (the power geography). Brand's Forge, Fenn's Fletchery & Simples, Pell's Bakery, Marsh's General Store, the Sleeping Ox and the Bridgeward College are in the lane scene. Building shells are solid masses with a doorway and a vestibule; the interiors are later beads, so each door is a locked wooden door (lock town-closed) with the hint 'Closed'. The mine road (south wall, exit-mine-road) is an open doorway with a signpost and the mine-road-gate transition into the Deepworks (arrive-from-deepworks stands inside the wall; mw-e26.2). The priory road (east wall, exit-priory-road) is still a planned edge stub: a doorway with a locked door (lock road-not-open) and a signpost, tagged planned:<bead>; the way into the Briarwood is the lane's woodside path. A new scene load (?scene=briar-glen-green) starts the player in Market Green (player-start, the perf budget's viewpoint).",
